# PR build, attach & verify (mandatory)

<!--
HOW TO USE THIS TEMPLATE
Copy to .cursor/rules/pr-artifact-verify.mdc only if your project produces an artifact a human
will install or deploy (mobile app, desktop binary, container image, static site). Replace every
<placeholder> with the real command. Delete this rule for pure libraries.
-->

Whenever you open (or push a build-affecting change to) a Pull Request, do all three of the following
before calling the PR "ready". Do not skip any step.

1. **Build** the release artifact.
2. **Attach** it to the PR as a downloadable asset and link it in the PR body.
3. **Verify** it on the target (device, emulator, container, staging URL): install, launch, capture evidence.

## 1. Build

```
<build command, e.g. a release build with source-map upload disabled for local runs>
```

Output: `<artifact path>`. The build takes minutes and emits a long log — run it in a **throwaway
subagent** that returns `BUILD OK/FAIL` + the last ~10 lines on failure + the artifact path. The
parent never ingests the log.

## 2. Attach

For a private repo, a downloadable-from-PR link means a **pre-release asset** (one tag per PR):

```
gh release create <artifact-tag>-pr-<N> "<artifact path>" --prerelease --title "Artifact for PR #<N>" --notes "Sideload build for PR #<N>."
# on later pushes to the same PR, replace the asset:
gh release upload <artifact-tag>-pr-<N> "<artifact path>" --clobber
```

Then add or update a **Test artifact** section in the PR body linking the release tag.

## 3. Verify on the target

```
<install command>
<launch command>
<evidence capture — screenshot / health-check / smoke-test command>
```

- **Prove the installed artifact is the one you built** (version string, hash, build timestamp)
  before trusting any pass or fail. A stale install is the most common cause of phantom bugs.
- Capture and inspect evidence **inside the subagent**; return a one-line description and a verdict,
  never the raw image or log, to the parent.
- Record the manual steps that cannot be automated in the PR's "Manual verification" checklist.

## Notes

- Changes visible only in a native build (icons, splash, native config) make steps 1 and 3 mandatory, not optional.
- Full runbook and gotchas for the target environment: `docs/<RUNBOOK>.md`.
